        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(safeguard): resolve compaction provider/model before registering runtime",
        "body": "Fixes #57901.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nSafeguard auto-compaction registered and preferred the active session model even when `agents.defaults.compaction.model` selected a different summarization model. That made the documented override ineffective in normal embedded runs; an unresolved override could also degrade to `model: undefined` without explaining which configured target failed.\n\n## Summary\n\nSafeguard auto-compaction now honors `agents.defaults.compaction.model` when embedded extensions register their runtime state.\n\n- Reuse `resolveEmbeddedCompactionTarget` before safeguard registration.\n- Resolve the selected provider/model through the active `ModelRegistry`, including alias/configured-model support.\n- Forward auth-profile, harness-runtime, and `modelSelectionLocked` inputs from both normal runs and explicit compaction runs.\n- Prefer the registered compaction model over `ctx.model` inside the safeguard hook.\n- Preserve locked native-harness sessions on their pinned model.\n- When a configured override cannot be resolved, emit a warning and retain the active session model instead of silently registering `model: undefined`.\n- Use the resolved compaction model's context window.\n- Remove the PR-only proof script and unrelated collateral churn; the PR now changes six focused source/test files.\n\n## Behavior\n\nFor a normal embedded run, the configured compaction target is resolved through the same shared resolver used by explicit compaction. A provider switch drops the session's provider-specific auth profile. If selection is locked to a native harness, the configured override is intentionally ignored.\n\nFor the explicit `/compact` path, the caller has already resolved and loaded the compaction target. Registration detects that the target matches and keeps that loaded model.\n\nThe safeguard hook now uses:\n\n```ts\nconst model = runtime?.model ?? ctx.model;\n```\n\nThat lets a configured compaction model win while preserving the session model as the no-override or unresolved-override fallback.\n\n## Evidence\n\nValidated on the synchronized merge tree:\n\n- PR head: `8c1ad51b4ba34ec1d19d2c389f149b9ea0602925`\n- Main cutoff / second parent: `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e`\n- Final diff: 6 files, +277/-17\n\nChecks:\n\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` — passed\n- Core test TypeScript project (`test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.json`) — passed\n- Focused Vitest suites — 4 files, 154 tests passed:\n  - `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner.extensions.test.ts`\n  - `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/compaction-runtime-context.test.ts`\n  - `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/extensions.test.ts`\n  - `src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-safeguard.test.ts`\n- `oxfmt --check` on all six changed files — passed\n- `oxlint --deny-warnings` on all six changed files — passed\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n\nThe affected `src/agents` full-core lint shard also passed. The full repository-wide lint command was not completed end-to-end locally after upstream moved during validation; CI remains the authoritative full gate.\n\n## Testing scope\n\nNo live provider API call was made. Regression coverage exercises target resolution, provider-switch auth handling, native-harness model locking, runtime registration, unresolved-model warning/fallback, and the safeguard summarizer receiving the runtime-selected model.\n",
        "branch": "fix/57901-safeguard-compaction-model",
